---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import VlanTags from "../../components/nova/xf/VlanTags.astro";
import { zones, rules, aliases, networkEvidence } from "../../data/network";
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const segments=zones.filter(z=>z.kind==="VLAN");
---
<BaseLayout title="Network" description="Follow Nova Corp's five VLANs, WireGuard tunnel, ordered firewall rules and protected company services." breadcrumbs={[{label:"Map",href:"map/"},{label:"Network"}]}>
<section class="page-head"><div class="container">
 <div class="eyebrow">Network / Company traffic</div>
 <h1>Where can a company computer connect?</h1>
 <p class="lead" style="margin-top:18px">pfSense sits between Nova Corp's networks. The VLANs say where each system lives, and the firewall rules, read in order, decide which connections cross. Some rules are still broader than they should be, and this page says which.</p>
 <div class="button-row" style="margin-top:25px"><a class="btn" href={base+"network/zones/client/"}>Follow an employee request →</a><a class="btn ghost" href={base+"network/rules/"}>Read the firewall rules in order</a></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container">
<VlanTags />
 <div class="stats-strip" style="margin:0 0 36px"><div class="stat"><b>{segments.length}</b><span>VLANs</span></div><div class="stat"><b>{rules.length}</b><span>Firewall rules</span></div><div class="stat"><b>{aliases.length}</b><span>Rule aliases</span></div></div>
 <div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Network areas</div><h2>How the lab is divided</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={base+"network/rules/"}>All rules →</a></div>
 <div class="area-grid">{zones.filter(z=>z.slug!=="vpn_remote").map(z=><a class="area-card" href={base+"network/zones/"+z.slug+"/"} style={"--accent:"+(z.slug==="vpn_remote"?"#0F766E":z.slug==="client"?"#7C3AED":"#2563EB")}>
   <div class="number"><span>{z.kind}</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></div><h3>{z.name}</h3>
   <p>{z.purpose}</p><span class="arrow-label">Open this network →</span>
 </a>)}</div>
 <div class="grid-main" style="margin-top:30px">
  <div class="paper panel"><p class="kicker">A protection I tested</p><h3 style="margin:12px 0">An employee PC cannot open the firewall's admin page.</h3><p class="muted" style="margin-top:11px">On the CLIENT network, two block rules sit ahead of a broad allow. After I added them (CR-015), I tested that the admin pages were blocked and that DNS, sign-in, file shares and internet still worked.</p><a class="evidence-link" href={base+"network/zones/client/"}>Follow the CLIENT rules →</a></div>
  <div class="paper panel"><p class="kicker">Not done yet</p><h3 style="margin:12px 0">Having VLANs is not the same as least privilege.</h3><p class="muted" style="margin-top:11px">The MGMT, INFRA, APP and DMZ networks still have broad pass rules. Isolating privileged administration is the next planned change, CR-016.</p><a class="evidence-link" href={base+"network/rules/"}>Explore the rule order →</a></div>
 </div>
 <div class="note" style="margin-top:28px">The lab has five VLANs: MGMT 10, INFRA 20, APP 30, CLIENT 40 and DMZ 50. <a href={base+"reference/explore/NETWORK/"}>Read the documented architecture ↗</a></div>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
